// ANONYMOUS TOKENS (#215). `string`, `number` and `object` above were declared
// here as TYPE_PRIMITIVE and were DEAD: javascript_types.def is #included at
// the top of this file and declares the same three strings as literals, and an
// unordered_map initialiser list is first-wins, so javascript's entries won and
// ast_type_map('typescript') reported LITERAL_STRING for `string`. They are
// moved to the anonymous table, which is the declaration they were always
// describing -- in `let s: string`, `string` is the anonymous type keyword,
// while the named `string` rule is the literal "x". See
// scripts/audit_anon_token_collisions.py.
//
// NOTE: 82 of this file's 183 DEF_TYPE entries are shadowed the same way.
// Tracked separately; only the three colliding ones are in scope for #215.
